(*
De-recursify Phase 3 — home_ctx-across-stacks validation.

Fiber A's entry block lexically captures an outer temp (`shared`, a slot of
this main:args: activation, which lives on the MAIN Stack and stays live for
the whole run since `concurrency run` is called from within main:args:).
Fiber A reads `shared` once, yields (suspending on its OWN Stack, a
different heap Stack object than the main Stack), then reads `shared` again
after being resumed.

Between A's two reads, fiber B — on a THIRD Stack — runs and MUTATES the
same captured `shared` slot. This proves more than "a fiber resumes at the
right pc": it proves the block's `home_ctx` (an absolute, base-relative
pointer into the spawner's live Stack — see frame_abi.h) resolves to the
SAME live storage location regardless of which Stack is currently
executing, and that a mutation made from a completely different Stack (B)
is visible when a suspended fiber (A) resumes and re-reads through its own
home_ctx chain. A broken cross-stack home_ctx (stale/misrouted after the
switch) would read a wrong, stale, or corrupted value for the second read
instead of the mutated 99.

expect:
before10
mutated
after99
done
*)
class FiberCaptureTest usingPlatform: platform concurrency: concurrency = () (
  public main: platform2 args: args = (
    | shared |
    shared:: 10.
    concurrency spawn: [
      ('before' , shared printString) println.
      concurrency yield.
      ('after' , shared printString) println ].
    concurrency spawn: [
      shared:: 99.
      'mutated' println.
      concurrency yield ].
    concurrency run.
    'done' println.
    ^ 0
  )
) : (
  public packageUsing: manifest = ( ^ self new )
)
